To make tool calls execute sequentially (one at a time) when the model generates multiple tool calls in a single step, set `toolCallConcurrency: 1` in your `generateText` call. This ensures later calls can observe side effects from earlier ones [7].

```ts
import { generateText, tool } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

const result = await generateText({
  model: 'anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5',
  tools: {
    // your tools here
  },
  prompt: 'Update the file, then read it.',
  toolCallConcurrency: 1, // run tools one at a time
});
```

To force the model to call a specific tool, use the `toolChoice` option with `{ type: 'tool', toolName: 'yourToolName' }`:

```ts
import { generateText, tool } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

const result = await generateText({
  model: "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5",
  tools: {
    weather: tool({
      description: 'Get the weather in a location',
      inputSchema: z.object({
        location: z.string().describe('The location to get the weather for'),
      }),
      execute: async ({ location }) => ({
        location,
        temperature: 72 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 21) - 10,
      }),
    }),
  },
  toolChoice: {
    type: 'tool',
    toolName: 'weather', // Force the weather tool to be used
  },
  prompt: 'What is the weather in San Francisco?',
});
```

